+# The Daily Grind
+
+Run `pnpm start` to serve the site and `pnpm test` for automated tests.
+
+## WebMCP
+
+The page registers three client-side tools with `document.modelContext`, falling
+back to `navigator.modelContext` for older implementations:
+
+| Tool | Input | Behavior |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `get_seasonal_favorites` | `{}` | Returns the displayed coffee names, descriptions, detail URLs, and destination IDs. |
+| `list_destinations` | `{}` | Returns the existing site destinations and their URLs. |
+| `open_destination` | `{ "destination": "menu" }` | Navigates the current tab to a listed destination. |
+
+Tools use the page's existing content and links. Navigation accepts only listed,
+same-origin HTTP(S) links. Logout is excluded. Opening `order-online` follows the
+existing ordering link; it does not create an order. This repository contains
+only the homepage; the linked routes still require the application's server.
+
+A browser or agent integration supporting WebMCP is required for tool discovery.
+Browsers without that API continue to display the page normally. Registration
+failures are caught and logged without interrupting the page. No polyfill or
+external service is installed. See the [WebMCP specification and explainer](https://github.com/webmachinelearning/webmcp)
+for browser-mediated discovery and invocation.
+
+Automated tests exercise tool callbacks and registration with a mocked DOM/API;
+they do not verify a native browser's WebMCP implementation.
